                <pb facs="0710" n="596" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg596"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.60K/124: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Danzig</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Danzig</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-16T12:00:00+01:00">April 16,
                        1931—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 16—9 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The Department’s April 15, 5 p.m., has been received.</p>
                <p>Invitation will not be accepted and probably will not be issued as the Senate is
                    reported to be unwilling to accept the proposal.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
